1
00:00:00,120 --> 00:00:05,600
In posterior-canal BPPV, displaced otoconia enter the posterior semicircular canal.

2
00:00:05,650 --> 00:00:11,547
Inside the right temporal bone, the posterior canal arches posterolaterally behind the utricle.

3
00:00:11,787 --> 00:00:17,331
Dense otoconia settle at the lowest point of the right posterior canal near the posterior ampulla.

4
00:00:17,381 --> 00:00:23,347
Sequential head rotations use gravity to guide the particles around the canal, through the common crus, and into the utricle.

5
00:00:23,587 --> 00:00:29,707
Step 1: Sit upright with a shoulder pillow behind the upper back and turn the head 45° right.

6
00:00:29,757 --> 00:00:36,347
Turning the head 45° right aligns the right posterior semicircular canal with the plane of recline.

7
00:00:36,587 --> 00:00:44,195
Step 2: Maintaining the 45° right turn, recline onto the shoulder pillow with 20–30° neck extension.

8
00:00:44,245 --> 00:00:52,447
Gravity pulls the otoconia away from the ampulla toward the posterior canal apex. Hold 30–60 seconds.

9
00:00:52,687 --> 00:01:00,135
Step 3: Without lifting the head, rotate 90° left to face 45° left while maintaining neck extension.

10
00:01:00,185 --> 00:01:08,213
Gravity guides the otoconia over the superior arch into the common crus. Hold 30–60 seconds.

11
00:01:08,453 --> 00:01:15,869
Step 4: Roll onto the left shoulder and turn the head another 90° left until the nose points 45° down.

12
00:01:15,919 --> 00:01:23,913
The common crus now points steeply downward, draining the otoconia toward the utricle. Hold 30–60 seconds.

13
00:01:24,153 --> 00:01:29,921
Step 5: Keeping the chin slightly tucked, slowly return the patient to an upright sitting position.

14
00:01:29,971 --> 00:01:36,180
Otoconia repositioned → maneuver complete. Particles exit into the utricle; if posterior-canal BPPV is the cause, vertigo should resolve.

15
00:01:36,420 --> 00:01:42,972
Clinical Summary: (1) Shoulder pillow for 20–30° extension; (2) Never lift the head during the Step 3 turn.

16
00:01:43,022 --> 00:01:50,080
(3) Hold each step 30–60 seconds so the otoconia completely settle along the canal pathway.

